<article class="env-lemma" id="04NK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04NK">Lemma <span data-tag="04NK">35.33.7</span>.</a> Let $r \in \{ 0, 1, 2, \ldots , \infty \} $. The property of morphisms of germs </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{P}_ r((X, x) \to (S, s)) \Leftrightarrow \text{trdeg}_{\kappa (s)} \kappa (x) = r  \]
</div>
  <p> is étale local on the source-and-target. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Given a diagram as in Definition <a href="/tag/04NB" data-tag="04NB">35.33.1</a> we obtain the following diagram of local homomorphisms of local rings 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{O}_{U', u'} &  \mathcal{O}_{V', v'} \ar[l] \\  \mathcal{O}_{U, u} \ar[u] &  \mathcal{O}_{V, v} \ar[l] \ar[u] }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Note that the vertical arrows are localizations of étale ring maps, in particular they are unramified (see Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/00U0" data-tag="00U0">10.143</a>). Hence $\kappa (u')/\kappa (u)$ and $\kappa (v')/\kappa (v)$ are finite separable field extensions. Thus we have $\text{trdeg}_{\kappa (v)} \kappa (u) = \text{trdeg}_{\kappa (v')} \kappa (u)$ which proves the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>